= The Death of Friedrich Naumann

<img src="img/cool_image.webp" style="float:right; margin-left:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:220px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:5px solid #000000ff;"> <br> Our chairman and <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">**Ge**</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">**rma**</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">**ny**</span>'s most influential <span style="color: var(--lvp-colour);">liberal</span> intellectual has passed away, one month after our first congress... He had just retreated to the Baltic sea to recover from overwork in the National Assembly and war-related malnutrition, when he suffered a stroke in Travemünde. 

It is a tragic event, especially with many of our prominent members once having been students or even associates of Naumann. For the party, we have lost our most unifying leader and created a void in the rank and file that we haven't prepared to solve. Carl Wilhelm Petersen is elected provisional chairman of the party, and an exaordinary party congress is scheduled at December to determine the new chairman and to draft the official party programme of the DDP.

> *"The idea of liberalism has to be recreated. In the course of time it has lost so much of its clarity and attraction that it first has to rise like a new dawn in front of the people."*

- Friedrich Naumann

- @sad: He will be missed.

@sad

Indeed.
